[al:新概念英语第三册]
[ti:4. The Double Life of Alfred Bloggs]
[00:00.540] Passage 4. | 第四篇文章。
[00:01.900] The double life of Alfred Bloggs. | 艾尔弗雷德·布洛格斯的双重生活。
[00:05.350] These days, people who do manual work often receive far more money than clerks who work in offices. | 如今，从事体力劳动的人挣的钱往往比办公室职员多得多。
[00:12.795] People who work in offices are frequently referred to as white-collar workers, | 办公室职员常被称为白领工人，
[00:17.600] for the simple reason that they usually wear a collar and tie to go to work. | 原因很简单，他们上班时通常会穿衬衫打领带。
[00:21.860] Such is human nature that a great many people are often willing to sacrifice higher pay | 人的天性使然，许多人常常愿意牺牲更高的薪水，
[00:28.035] for the privilege of becoming white-collar workers. | 以换取成为白领工人的特权。
[00:31.105] This can give rise to curious situations. | 这可能会导致一些奇怪的情况。
[00:34.440] As it did in the case of Alfred Bloggs, | 艾尔弗雷德·布洛格斯就是如此，
[00:37.195] who worked as a dustman for the Elsmere Corporation. | 他曾为埃尔斯米尔公司做清洁工。
[00:41.150] When he got married, Alf was too embarrassed to say anything to his wife about his job. | 当他结婚时，艾尔夫太不好意思告诉妻子他的工作。
[00:47.035] He simply told her that he worked for the corporation. | 他只是告诉她，他在那家公司工作。
[00:50.325] Every morning, he left home dressed in a fine black suit. | 每天早上，他都穿着一套漂亮的黑色西装离开家。
[00:54.935] He then changed into overalls and spent the next eight hours as a dustman. | 然后他换上工作服，接下来八小时都做清洁工。
[01:00.225] Before returning home at night, | 晚上回家之前，
[01:02.670] he took a shower and changed back into his suit. | 他会洗个澡，然后换回他的西装。
[01:05.905] Alf did this for over two years. | 艾尔夫这样做超过两年了。
[01:08.910] And his fellow dustmen kept his secret. | 他的清洁工同事们替他保守了这个秘密。
[01:11.775] Alf's wife has never discovered that she married a dustman, | 艾尔夫的妻子从未发现她嫁给了一个清洁工，
[01:15.740] and she never will. | 她也永远不会知道。
[01:17.455] For Alf has just found another job. | 因为艾尔夫刚刚找到了另一份工作。
[01:20.185] He will soon be working in an office as a junior clerk. | 他很快就会在办公室里担任初级职员。
[01:24.055] He will be earning only half as much as he used to, | 他挣的钱将只有以前的一半，
[01:27.325] but he feels that his rise in status | 但他觉得他的地位提升
[01:30.010] is well worth the loss of money. | 非常值得损失的金钱。
[01:33.080] From now on, | 从现在起，
[01:35.225] he will wear a suit all day, | 他将整天穿着西装，
[01:37.435] and others will call him Mr. Bloggs, | 别人会叫他布洛格斯先生，
[01:40.550] not Alf. | 而不是艾尔夫。